      "writtenOn": "2024-12-23T02:05:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we try a more tightly scoped `fd` with a single `try catch` for all IOs:\n\n```\nfinal ByteBuffer resp;\ntry (FileDescriptor fd \u003d NetlinkUtils.netlinkSocketForProto(NETLINK_ROUTE, SOCKET_RECV_BUFSIZE)) {\n  sendMessage(fd, msg);\n  resp \u003d NetlinkUtils.recvMessage(fd);\n} catch (ErrnoException | InterruptedIOException e) {\n  Log.w();\n  return null;\n}\n``` \n\nThis avoids having a dangling `fd` variable later in the function.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 514,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 531,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "678a1d3bb3d73f52eca57e80ec4416d793f0c9a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
