      "writtenOn": "2024-12-23T07:13:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes we need to close this.\n\nBTW one cool improvement here would be to use a subclass or wrapper class of FileDescriptor which implements https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/lang/AutoCloseable.html and then it will get autoclosed when declared as a resource in a try catch. This seems to me much better pattern and as close to RAII as we can get in Java.",
      "parentUuid": "53c96a54_13a4a407",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 514,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 531,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "678a1d3bb3d73f52eca57e80ec4416d793f0c9a9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
