      "lineNbr": 531,
      "author": {
        "id": 1962260
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-24T07:33:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for noticing this.\n\n\u003e subclass or wrapper class of FileDescriptor which implements AutoCloseable\n\nThis sounds good, maybe something like:\n```\nsendMessage(FileDescriptor fd, byte[] message) {\n    try (FileOutputStream fos \u003d new FileOutputStream(fd)) {\n        fos.write(message);\n        fos.flush();\n    } catch (IOException e) {\n        // Err handling\n    }\n}\n```\n?\n\nMaybe it is better to do this in a spearate patch other than this.\nAdded fd close for now. (Did not use try resource since need to close it in `finally` following the style of other fd usage in `NetlinkUtils`)",
      "parentUuid": "8e19945a_ff20843f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 514,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 531,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "678a1d3bb3d73f52eca57e80ec4416d793f0c9a9",
