      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T06:58:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed this should be a separate patch. For now doing the close in `finally` sounds good.\n\n\u003e maybe something like sendMessage(FileDescriptor fd, byte[] message)\n\nI would go one step further and move the creation of the FD directly inside the helper function. This completely encapsulates the resource creation and destruction.\n\nBasically we need a version of `sendOneShotKernelMessage()` that returns something.\n\nBy using overloads we can return the correct type based on the input msg type, instead of having a byte[] input:\n\n```\nRtNetlinkLinkMessage sendOneShotRtNlMsg(RtNetlinkLinkMessage request);\n// etc\n// there is no example for other protocol than rtnl in this file.\n```",
